WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.835
Nico Reyes: Ooh, that smells good!

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:03.668
Ian Burke: It smells like...

00:00:03.668 --> 00:00:04.501
Meredith Cash: Rubber.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:07.000
Benji Jones: This one looks and feels

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.760
like it's not gonna taste good.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.660
It's like peanut butter in your mouth.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.460
That's me and a few hungry coworkers

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.989
tasting 13 different veggie burgers.

00:00:17.989 --> 00:00:21.100
Ian: Nope, nope, nope, nope.
It tastes like broccoli.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.130
Benji: Today, you can find veggie burgers

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.970
pretty much everywhere.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.663
And some brands are even
trying to give real beef

00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:29.260
a run for its money.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.170
But how do they all stack up?

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.430
And are they really that much
healthier than the real thing?

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.353
That's what I set out to discover.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.180
Let's go hunt some veggie burgers!

00:00:44.506 --> 00:00:45.806
There are so many options!

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.120
In grocery stores, I
found your typical brands,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.290
like Boca and MorningStar.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.620
And at fast-food chains,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.950
I picked up the Impossible
Burger and the Beyond Burger.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.782
And after that, there was
nothing left to do but eat

00:01:00.782 --> 00:01:03.763
and rank which burgers reigned supreme.

00:01:06.203 --> 00:01:09.043
Kyle Desiderio: This is
like re-re-re-refried beans.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.238
Benji: Spoiler, that
brand wasn't a favorite.

00:01:13.238 --> 00:01:15.940
Nico: This is beans on,
like, the second week.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.090
Beans.
Kyle: Oh, God.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.800
Benji: In the end, six
volunteers, including me,

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.240
tasted all 13 veggie burgers.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.640
Plus, one real beef burger,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.670
which I tossed in for good measure.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.110
We scored each burger on its overall look,

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.950
smell, taste, and texture,

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.683
and on how it compared
to a real beef burger.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:39.020
Ian: That's like wet
sand. It just fell apart.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.930
Meredith: You don't
need teeth to eat this.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.960
Benji: Overall, the veggie burgers...

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.600
well, they weren't very popular.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.577
But one did stand out:

00:01:47.577 --> 00:01:50.020
the Impossible Burger from Burger King.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.620
Commercial: With a patty
made from plants, no beef.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.530
Get it while it lasts.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.363
Nico: That's a burger.

00:01:55.363 --> 00:01:57.868
Holy moly!
Kyle: That's really good.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.470
This is the best one by far.
Nico: In terms of taste.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.590
I thought we were gonna
be sad this whole time.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.180
Benji: It got a near-perfect score

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.687
in the first category.

00:02:04.687 --> 00:02:06.340
It even beat out the beef burger,

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:09.290
and it was just shy of the
beef burger in the second one.

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:11.440
Which makes sense, because, you know,

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.214
beef should win in a category about

00:02:13.214 --> 00:02:15.222
how meat-like something is.

00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:17.310
The only other veggie
burger that came close

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.930
in either category was Gardein.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.050
But as you can see,

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.870
it was still several points
away from Impossible.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.430
And there was something else I noticed.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.370
Many of the low-scoring burgers

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.463
were knocked for smelling
and tasting artificial.

00:02:32.879 --> 00:02:35.120
Meredith: No. I taste chemicals.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.480
This tastes like plastic,

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.770
like, up in the back of your palate.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.490
And I can't get past that.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.680
Ian: It smells like Clorox.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.110
Benji: And that got me thinking,

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.780
are these burgers actually good for you?

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.500
After all, eating healthy
is one of the main reasons

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.370
why people avoid red meat.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.630
So I asked a registered dietitian.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.490
Today we're gonna talk
about veggie burgers,

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.210
so I thought it was
appropriate that we would get

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.540
one of the new Impossible
Burgers from Burger King.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.840
Lisa Moskovitz: I don't
regularly eat Burger King,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.040
or at least I don't want
anyone to know that I (laughs).

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.130
Benji: After I was scolded

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.370
for making a dietician eat fast food,

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:11.531
we got into it.

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:15.501
Lisa: Hm.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:16.392
Benji: From a health point of view,

00:03:16.392 --> 00:03:17.967
what should you consider?

00:03:17.967 --> 00:03:19.570
Lisa: If it's gonna be
the source of protein,

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.650
then you definitely wanna
look at the protein content.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:22.933
Benji: She said to shoot for:

00:03:22.933 --> 00:03:26.332
Lisa: 15 to 30 grams of
protein per veggie burger.

00:03:26.332 --> 00:03:28.310
Benji: So, how did our burgers measure up?

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.760
Let's take a look.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.650
As you can see, a lot of
them had plenty of protein,

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.780
like Dr. Praeger's. Twenty-eight grams!

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.540
That's way more than even the beef burger.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:41.710
And while a lot of veggie-burger
protein comes from soy,

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:43.910
Moskovitz said that's not a problem.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.340
Lisa: Now, the consensus
is pretty much that

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.170
not only is soy not bad for you,

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:50.600
but it actually can fight off cancer.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.490
It can be really good for your heart,

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.415
and as a vegetarian and
definitely as a vegan,

00:03:55.415 --> 00:03:58.220
it's a really good source
of complete protein.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.970
Benji: You should also
be mindful of sodium.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.820
Lisa: The average healthy adult
should try to keep it under

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.070
2,300 milligrams of sodium per day.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.810
So, if the veggie burger is clocking in

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.793
at over 600 to 700 milligrams of salt,

00:04:10.793 --> 00:04:13.010
you know, that's also
something to consider.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.210
Benji: Now, all 13 veggie burgers

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.310
did have more sodium than the beef patty.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.370
But they were still well
below that 600-milligram mark.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.610
And another nutrient to look out for is:

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.783
Lisa: Saturated fat.

00:04:24.783 --> 00:04:26.900
Especially if you have a history of

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.420
high cholesterol or any
sort of heart disease.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.113
If you can find one that has, like,

00:04:31.113 --> 00:04:33.223
less than 2 or 3 grams of saturated fat,

00:04:33.223 --> 00:04:34.310
that would be great.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.301
Benji: Here's where the
Impossible and Beyond burgers

00:04:36.301 --> 00:04:37.134
stood out.

00:04:37.134 --> 00:04:39.080
Unlike most of the other veggie burgers,

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:42.110
they had a similar amount
of saturated fat as beef.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:43.580
And that's at least partly why

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.330
they taste so much like the real thing.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.740
But there's one type of fat

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.000
that really sets veggie
burgers apart from real beef.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.560
And that's trans fat.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.950
Lisa: The one thing you'll
ever hear a dietician say

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.080
don't eat ever is trans fat.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.690
You know, everything in moderation,

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.970
except for trans fat.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.237
It increases your bad LDL cholesterol,

00:05:03.237 --> 00:05:05.500
and it decreases your
good HDL cholesterol.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.350
Benji: So, there's actually
good reason to believe

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.660
that veggie burgers are
healthier than meat.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.410
Especially considering that red meat

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.410
has been linked to some forms of cancer.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.980
But that doesn't mean veggie
burgers are healthy in general.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.600
Case in point, remember
that chemical taste?

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.640
Meredith: I taste chemicals.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.930
Benji: It might have something to do

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.497
with the dozens of ingredients
added to these burgers

00:05:25.497 --> 00:05:27.420
to make them taste like a beef patty.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.520
Lisa: If it has a ton of
ingredients, you know,

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.120
that's probably an issue.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.720
And if a lot of those things

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.858
a 5-year-old can't pronounce,

00:05:34.858 --> 00:05:36.500
then that's even more of an issue.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.090
Benji: I mean, I can't
even pronounce these.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:42.190
And how you prepare that
burger also matters.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.270
Lisa: Are you putting cheese on it?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:44.910
Are you putting a ton of
ketchup and mayonnaise?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.640
Are you having it on a white bun?

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.650
You know, that's also
something you wanna consider.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:52.267
Benji: In other words,
fast food is fast food.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.170
It is interesting, 'cause,
like, I look at this burger,

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.420
and I'm like, I am healthier
than the person next to me

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.290
eating this with meat.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.440
Lisa: Yes, it might be healthier,

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.890
but if you're eating this every day

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.756
and the guy next to you
is eating that beef burger

00:06:02.756 --> 00:06:03.970
once a month,

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.360
who's really healthier?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.906
Benji: Now, of course, there are reasons

00:06:06.906 --> 00:06:09.800
other than personal health
to choose veggie burgers.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.420
They have a smaller
environmental footprint

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.810
than beef, for example.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.350
And no cows were killed to make them.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.080
And if you are concerned
about your health,

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:20.010
just look for burgers with
a short list of ingredients.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.244
Or, better yet, make them yourself.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.593
Nick Fernandez: I eat almost everything.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.173
That's just terrible.

